#### Phase 3: Schema Registration (AWS Glue Schema Registry)

**Step 7: Schema Definition**

Create AVRO schema for topic:

```json
{
  "type": "record",
  "name": "ClaimSubmitted",
  "namespace": "com.gainwell.claims.adjudication.v1",
  "doc": "Event emitted when claim is submitted for adjudication",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "claimId",
      "type": "string",
      "doc": "Unique claim identifier"
    },
    {
      "name": "memberId",
      "type": "string",
      "doc": "Member identifier"
    },
    {
      "name": "submittedAt",
      "type": "long",
      "logicalType": "timestamp-millis",
      "doc": "Submission timestamp"
    },
    {
      "name": "claimAmount",
      "type": {
        "type": "bytes",
        "logicalType": "decimal",
        "precision": 10,
        "scale": 2
      },
      "doc": "Claim amount in USD"
    },
    {
      "name": "metadata",
      "type": {
        "type": "record",
        "name": "EventMetadata",
        "fields": [
          {"name": "eventId", "type": "string"},
          {"name": "eventTime", "type": "long"},
          {"name": "source", "type": "string"}
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Step 8: Schema Registration**

```bash
# Register schema in AWS Glue Schema Registry
aws glue create-schema \
  --schema-name "claims.adjudication.claim.submitted.v1-value" \
  --data-format AVRO \
  --compatibility BACKWARD \
  --schema-definition file://schemas/claim-submitted-v1.avsc \
  --tags Domain=claims,Compliance=HIPAA
```

